# The same policy as ../input.lg with the actor declared after the gates and
# the cords in reverse order, but the gates themselves in the same relative
# order (A, B, C, E, D). Verdicts and decision are unchanged (SPEC §7.5,
# rule 2); the §7.4 tie-break reads only the gates' declaration order, which
# is unchanged, so the log is the same as against ../input.lg: A, B, C, E, D.
gate  A grant a
gate  B grant a
gate  C
gate  E grant a
gate  D grant a
actor a
cord D -> master
cord E -> D
cord C -> D
cord B -> D
cord A -> E
cord A -> C
cord A -> B
cord a -> A
